Two Main Types of Searching Algorithms

Two Main Types of Searching AlgorithmsQ

1. Linear Search: The 'One-by-One' Method

What Is It?
Linear search is like looking for your lucky hoodie by picking up each piece of clothing one at a time and checking if it's the right one.
You start from the top of the pile and go through each item until you (hopefully) find it.

Efficiency:

. Time Complexity: O(n) - This means in the worst case, you might have to look through every single item. Great if you have only a few clothes, but not so great if you're a shopaholic.
Analogy: Remember the time you lost your phone, and you asked your friend to call it? Instead of hearing the ringtone right away, you had to check under every cushion and behind every piece of furniture - that's linear search for you!

2. Binary Search: The Smart Way

What Is It?
Now, what if your clothes were nicely folded and arranged by color (wishful thinking, right)? Instead of checking every item, you could
start in the middle, see if the hoodie is to your left or right, and quickly narrow down your search. This is Binary Search in action.

Efficiency:

. Time Complexity: O(log n) - Super-fast, but there's a catch - it only works if your data is already sorted (just like you need your clothes organized to find them easily).
